All done. Here's a summary of what was implemented:

**Bead simple-war-cuq.12 — ECS: Rewrite Entity System Rules**

The entire `Entity System Rules.md` was rewritten top-to-bottom using ECS concepts:

1. **Section 200 (Entities and Components)** — Replaced the old Entity/Tag model with Entity/Component/System. Added new subsections: 200.2 Components (Data vs Marker), 200.3 Marker Components (Tags), 200.4 Systems (table of core Systems), 200.5 Archetypes (summary table), 200.6 Object References (renumbered from old 200.3).

2. **Section 210 (Statline Component)** — Reframed all Characteristics as properties of the Statline Component. Systems (Combat System, Movement System, Morale System) are now explicitly named as the logic that reads/writes this data.

3. **Sections 220–230 (Items, Models)** — All Items and Models redefined as archetypes with explicit Component lists (AttackProfileComponent, ArmourComponent, ConsumableComponent, EquippedItemsComponent, DestructionStateComponent, etc.).

4. **Sections 240–270 (Units, Abilities, Commanders, Armies, Battleforces)** — Each redefined as an archetype with named Components (CompositionComponent, MoraleStateComponent, ZoneComponent, ValueComponent, AbilityRefsComponent, etc.).

5. **Glossary** — Expanded with ECS-specific entries (Component, System, Archetype, Data Component, Marker Component, Damage Instance, Attack/Defense Pipeline, etc.).

6. **Implementation Notes** — Refactored from per-type state lists to explicit Component definitions and a System Responsibilities table showing reads/writes.

7. **Cross-references** — Updated Terminology.md to reference renumbered rules (200.2→200.3, 200.3→200.6). All 210+ rule numbers unchanged, so no downstream breakage.

**Files changed**: `Entity System Rules.md`, `Terminology.md`, `.ralph-tui/progress.md`

